    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100">

                <pb facs="0206" n="96" xml:id="pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841D.51/163</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Irish Free State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-28"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 13.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 112</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction No. 26 dated April 16, 1928, directing the Legation to
                    address a formal communication to the Government of the Irish Free State on the
                    subject of the so-called Irish Republic Loans floated in the United States, in
                    an endeavor to ascertain the official attitude of the Government towards the
                    American subscribers to these loans.</p>
                <p>Upon receipt of this instruction the Legation duly forwarded a note to the
                    Minister for External Affairs, and I now beg to transmit herewith a copy, in
                    triplicate, of the Minister’s reply.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>F. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d100-a1.xml" xpointer="d100-a1"/>
            </div>
